### Adding new DetectorInfo classes and replacing existing ones
In case the implementation of some detector in **PandaRoot** has changed significantly, you can either update the existing **DetectorInfo** class to work with the new code or create a new **DetectorInfo** class to replace the old one.
This could look similar to this:
```c++
#include "TClonesArray.h"

#include "FairRootManager.h"
#include "FairRuntimeDb.h"
#include "FairPropagator.h"

#include "PndPidCandidate.h"
#include "PndPidDetectorInfo.h"

class PndPidSomeNewDetectorInfo : public PndPidDetectorInfo {
 protected:
  TClonesArray *fDetectorHits;
  TClonesArray *fSomeDifferentTypeOfHits;

  WhateverOtherAttributes fYouMightNeed;

 public:
  PndPidSomeNewDetectorInfo() {};
  ~PndPidSomeNewDetectorInfo() {};

  void Reset();
  virtual Int_t SetDetectorHits(FairRootManager *manager);
  virtual Bool_t Setup(FairRootManager *manager, FairPropagator *propagator, DetectorParams *params);
  virtual void SetupDebug(Bool_t debug_mode);
  virtual Bool_t GetInfo(PndTrack *track, PndPidCandidate *pidCand);

  ClassDef(PndPidSomeNewDetectorInfo, 1);
};
```
If replacing an existing **DetectorInfo** class you don't need to change anything within the **PidCorrelator**. After initializing the **PidCorrelator** just set the new **DetectorInfo** instead of the old version:
```c++
PndPidCorrelator *correlator = new PndPidCorrelator();

// new DetectorInfo, say it should replace PndPidDrcInfo
correlator->SetDrcInfo(new PndPidSomeNewDetectorInfo());
```

If you want to add a new class (like adding a new detector to the setup), you might need to account for that additional detector in the **PndPidCorrelator** code.

